<!DOCTYPE html>
<%# The langlets. mobile app shell. Dark-only by design (see the mockup), so the
    theme is hard-coded rather than read from the user's preference — a user who
    picked light mode on the web still gets the app's dark palette here.

    Never use `dark:` utilities in views rendered by this layout: the variant keys
    off this very attribute, so they'd be unconditionally on and the intent would
    be invisible. Use the app-* tokens directly. %>
<html lang="<%= current_translation_language&.iso_name || I18n.locale %>" dir="<%= current_translation_language&.rtl? ? 'rtl' : 'ltr' %>" data-theme="dark">
  <head>
    <%= render "layouts/head" %>
  </head>

  <%# data-native-tabs: the iOS app draws a native tab bar. The web view
      extends beneath it, so app-scroll-pad reserves the tab bar and safe-area
      clearance (see application.tailwind.css). %>
  <body class="bg-app-bg text-app-text font-app antialiased" <%= "data-native-tabs" if native_app? %>>
    <main class="min-h-dvh"
          data-controller="audio-cache"
          data-action="click->audio-cache#handleClick:capture audio-cache:play->audio-cache#playEvent audio-cache:preload->audio-cache#preloadEvent audio-cache:stop->audio-cache#stop">
      <%= yield %>
    </main>

    <% if params[:signed_out].present? %>
      <div data-controller="bridge--sign-out" hidden></div>
    <% end %>

    <%# Mirrors the Queue badge onto the native tab bar item, once per page
        load — the same freshness the web tab bar's badge gets. %>
    <% if native_app? %>
      <div data-controller="bridge--tab-badge"
           data-bridge--tab-badge-count-value="<%= @queue_badge_count.to_i %>"
           hidden></div>

      <%# Hands the APNs device token to the server: the native side has the
          token but no session, this side has the session but no token.
          `ask` gates the permission prompt — see App::BaseController#ask_for_push?.
          Registration itself is silent for anyone who already granted it, so the
          token refreshes on every launch. %>
      <div data-controller="bridge--push"
           data-bridge--push-ask-value="<%= ask_for_push? %>"
           data-bridge--push-endpoint-value="<%= app_device_tokens_path %>"
           hidden></div>
    <% end %>
  </body>
</html>
